 # Changelog
 
+## 2026-11-03 — Pure slices for QLT-05 workload fitness and NFR-07 diagnostics export (candidate branch, unwired)
+
+- Add `core/fitness.ts`: strict workload declaration parser, kernel judgement of a workload report against declared targets (smoke, missing, oversized, too deep, too few samples), a series bounded to 12 points keyed by receipt id and tagged by a kernel-observed environment, the consecutive-degradation rule of workload-receipt §5.5 and a trend report that carries the no-whole-application-claim sentence. `report-contradiction` is not implemented (independent review W3).
+- Add `core/diagnostics.ts`: allowlist projection of state, journal and host facts, redaction as a second layer that refuses and never edits, sorted-key text with a SHA-256 bundle hash and no clock, 500-call and 256 KB bounds, and a candidate OpenTelemetry mapping; the journal's explicit `unknown` is exported as written (TS §16). Every attribute name is an unverified candidate; no version is pinned.
+- Both modules are pure and called by nothing. No capped module, schema, reason code or verb changed. R1 mapping unchanged (141 / 16 / 24); no `[QLT-05]` or `[NFR-07]` tag, because the wired examples are not built.
+- Files: `packages/kernel/src/core/fitness.ts`, `packages/kernel/src/core/diagnostics.ts`, `packages/kernel/test/fitness.test.ts`, `packages/kernel/test/diagnostics.test.ts`, `specs/plan.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`.
+- Tests: 48 fitness and 32 diagnostics tests pass on Windows (Node 24), including fast-check properties. `typecheck`, `lint-arch`, `lint-skills`, `lint-quality` and `coverage` pass.
+
 ## 2026-11-03 — Release-notes tool and release workflow candidates (LFC-02, ENG-07)
 
 - Add `tools/release-notes.ts`: drafts release notes from repository facts (changed paths per disclosure item, R1 mapping, open gates, known limits) and `--check` fails while a section lacks a written statement. Notes location assumed to be `docs/release/notes/v<version>.md`; the specs leave it open.
